WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.688
Raj: The review queue is my main blocker. The change is up for review already.

2
00:00:05.688 --> 00:00:11.641
Lukas: I've got bandwidth at eleven this morning. I can't promise approval before reading it.

3
00:00:11.641 --> 00:00:18.745
Priya: Just to confirm, eleven is review start, right? What's the ETA for initial feedback?

4
00:00:18.745 --> 00:00:25.705
Anika: My integration branch depends on its output shape. I can still prepare the adapter tests.

5
00:00:25.705 --> 00:00:34.226
Hannah: Keep the interface description beside the change. Reviewers shouldn't reverse-engineer the expected output.

6
00:00:34.226 --> 00:00:41.426
Raj: Okay, I'll add that description before eleven. Maybe ten minutes for the example outputs.

7
00:00:41.426 --> 00:00:48.411
Lukas: Initial feedback should arrive before lunch. Larger design questions may need a separate discussion.

8
00:00:48.411 --> 00:00:55.419
Priya: We'll circle back at the afternoon checkpoint. Don't mark the review complete before feedback.

9
00:00:55.419 --> 00:01:03.268
Hannah: I can review test clarity in parallel. That doesn't replace Lukas's implementation review.

10
00:01:03.268 --> 00:01:11.500
Anika: Good, I'll prepare integration fixtures meanwhile. That keeps progress moving without assuming interface approval.

